  "goodToKnow": "Die Astronomie is astronomy; der Astronom (weak noun) is an astronomer. Johannes Kepler, working in Prague and Linz, discovered the laws of planetary motion in the early 1600s, and Germany's Max Planck institutes are leaders in astronomy today. Astronomisch also means astronomical: astronomische Preise. Don't confuse it with die Astrologie (astrology, horoscopes). It has no plural."
